        "heading_H4MGMB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Treating Fresh Spills",
            "heading_size": "hd3",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_highlight_style": "none"
          }
        },
        "text_kBCVH8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2>If an accidental spill happens, don’t panic. The key is to act quickly, but make sure to not make the stain worse with a potential misstep. Always begin by blotting and removing as much of the stain as you can with a cloth or paper towelUse a cloth dampened with warm water and club soda to treat the affected area. Be gentle and do not rub too harshly, as this can work the stain deeper into the fibersIf you have a stubborn stain on your hands, you can try using a mild or natural soap. Never use harsh over-the-counter chemicals or cleaning products. Once the stain has lifted, use a dry, clean white cloth to blot away any excess waterIf the stain persists, give us a call to schedule a professional cleaning</h2>",
            "text_size": "text-base"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_H4MGMB",
        "text_kBCVH8"
